id: PL-PP-011
item: mistake-fixing guidance or skill, role-specific
context: keeper direction (2026-11-01, from the P7 post-pickup incident): agents will make mistakes; plan a tool or skill for guidance on FIXING one — with ROLE-SPECIFIC variants, because mistake scope and impact differ radically (a task-orc mistake is worktree-scoped and resets cheaply; an orchestrator mistake may span a phase and consumed inputs; a planner mistake is law/records that OTHER ROLES MAY HAVE CONSUMED — recovery must verify consumer state, never assume it, and reconcile idempotently). Open for the unpark session, filed open: form (one skill with role sections vs per-role guidance); the universal spine (disclose → assess blast radius via git/status/consumer check → fix the record → reconcile consumers → log the lesson); hooks into the loop or verify; relation to safety lines and the two-size resets
unpark-when: when the keeper wants the session or with the roles-writing guidance work. CALIBRATION INPUT (2026-11-01, P7 sign-off arc): the escalation rules are this skill's decision table — escalate a decision with a live keeper-owned alternative (direction/law/tiering), after two failed fix rounds, on genuine conflict; never as artifact-reading, bundled mega-questions, or approval-without-alternatives. Full arc in git history (the suggestion file was deleted 2026-11-01 after its law landed in both role files).
