resolved: -

id: PL-PO-002
item: `bee init` from a worktree registers the worktree's skills dir
context: surfaced by P3's first dispatch: `bee init` derives the skills path from its own location, so running it from any worktree would register that worktree's `skills/` instead of the main checkout's. Behavior unchanged in P3 (only test expectations were made location-neutral). Open question for the keeper: should `bee init` resolve the main checkout via `--git-common-dir` like `scripts/task.sh` does?
unpark-when: when the keeper rules on worktree-aware registration (natural home: a later `bee` CLI phase).
origin: po
opened: -
resolved: 2026-11-01T17:26:35+11:00
how: keeper-ruled 2026-11-01 (P6 planning): green-fields-first — init creates git if none; worktree = edge — resolve via common dir (branch, not worktree) + tell the runner to return to the main worktree and branch there if needed

